# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  .env.example  –  Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your values.
#
#  IMPORTANT: Never commit ".env" to Git.  It contains secrets.
#             The .gitignore in this project already excludes ".env".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Google Sheets Integration (Step 5 of GOOGLE_SETUP.md) ─────────────────────
#
# Replace every PASTE_... placeholder below with your real value, then save
# the file as ".env" (remove the ".example" part of the filename).
#
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_CREDENTIALS_FILE
#   Full path to the JSON key file you downloaded from Google Cloud Console.
#   Windows example:  C:\Users\YourName\Downloads\apartment-mgmt-abc123.json
#   Linux/macOS:      /home/yourname/apartment-mgmt-abc123.json
#   Use this for local / self-hosted setups.
#
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_CREDENTIALS_JSON  (alternative — for cloud deployments)
#   Paste the *entire contents* of the JSON key file as a single value.
#   Cloud platforms (Render, Railway, Heroku) cannot store files, so use this
#   instead of GOOGLE_SHEETS_CREDENTIALS_FILE.
#   Example:  {"type":"service_account","project_id":"...","private_key":"..."}
#   Leave blank if you are using GOOGLE_SHEETS_CREDENTIALS_FILE.
#
# GOOGLE_SHEET_*_ID
#   The Spreadsheet ID for each sheet.  Find it in the browser URL:
#     https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/YOUR_ID_IS_HERE/edit
#   Copy the long string between /d/ and /edit.
#
# GOOGLE_SHEET_USERS_ID  (optional but strongly recommended)
#   A dedicated Google Sheet that stores usernames and hashed passwords.
#   Passwords are stored as SHA-256 hashes — plain-text passwords are never
#   written.  When set, the app reads/writes user credentials from this sheet
#   so you can manage them centrally without accessing the server file system.
#   Required columns (Row 1 = header):
#     username | password_hash | role | name | flat | block | must_change_password | email
#   The ``email`` column is used for the "Forgot Password" feature.

GOOGLE_SHEETS_CREDENTIALS_FILE=PASTE_FULL_PATH_TO_YOUR_JSON_KEY_FILE
GOOGLE_SHEETS_CREDENTIALS_JSON=
GOOGLE_SHEET_USERS_ID=PASTE_SPREADSHEET_ID_FOR_USER_CREDENTIALS
GOOGLE_SHEET_CONTRIBUTIONS_ID=PASTE_SPREADSHEET_ID_FOR_MONTHLY_CONTRIBUTION
GOOGLE_SHEET_BALANCE_ID=PASTE_SPREADSHEET_ID_FOR_CURRENT_BALANCE_SHEET
GOOGLE_SHEET_CRDR_ID=PASTE_SPREADSHEET_ID_FOR_BALANCE_SHEET_CR_DR

# ── Optional app settings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PORT=5000
# FLASK_DEBUG=false
# SECRET_KEY=change-me-to-something-random

# ── Email (Forgot Password feature) ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# EMAIL_SENDER  (required for forgot-password to work)
#   The email address that password-reset emails are sent FROM.
#   For Gmail SMTP:  your Gmail address  (e.g. myapartment@gmail.com)
#   For SendGrid:    any address you have verified as a Sender Identity in SendGrid.
#
# ── Option A: SendGrid — recommended for cloud deployments ───────────────────
#   Works on every hosting platform, including those that block outbound SMTP
#   (e.g. Render free tier, Railway).  100 emails/day free.
#
#   Setup:
#     1. Sign up at https://sendgrid.com (free).
#     2. Go to Settings → API Keys → Create API Key (Mail Send permission).
#     3. Go to Settings → Sender Authentication → verify EMAIL_SENDER.
#     4. Set SENDGRID_API_KEY below.
#
# ── Option B: Gmail App Password — works for local / self-hosted setups ──────
#   EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD is a Gmail App Password (NOT your normal Gmail password).
#   Generate one at: https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#   (Requires 2-Step Verification on the Gmail account.)
#
#   The app tries SMTP port 465 (SSL) first, then port 587 (STARTTLS).
#   If your hosting platform blocks all outbound SMTP, use Option A or C.
#
# ── Option C: Google Workspace + Gmail API (advanced) ────────────────────────
#   If you are a Google Workspace admin and have configured domain-wide
#   delegation for the gmail.send scope on your service account, set:
#     EMAIL_USE_GMAIL_API=true
#   The app will then use the Gmail API (HTTPS) instead of SMTP.
#   Regular @gmail.com accounts cannot use this option.
#
# EMAIL_SENDER=myapartment@gmail.com
# SENDGRID_API_KEY=SG.xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx
# EMAIL_USE_GMAIL_API=false
